What happened... I fell through a trapdoor and landed on the Castle
level far from the stairs. As usual the two purple L's did not wait
more than two turns to appear next to me. I had a few charges in my
wand of lightning so that was no immediate problem. My first thought
was to scare them with my powerful +5 Frostbrand and while they left
to heal at the stairs to proceed to the stairs, but that didn't work
because they heal far too fast. It also turned out that my wand had
only three (or so) charges and writing in the dust while fighting
did cost me my cloak of protection from an arch-liches spell attack.
(Yeah, I know that I also could have died in that process.) So "plan
B" was to cowardly leave the level by confused teleport; but I did
not like that plan. I feared that if I re-enter the level I'll land
next to the stairs with one of the liches blocking it. Meanwhile
there were quite some summoned nasties, two Olog-hai and two purple
worms, a disenchanter, ettins, xorns, a couple of dragons - I even
thought that they must have been the Castle residents who escaped
the Castle somehow - an umber hulk and a lot of multiplying gremlins.
So I started my (final) "plan C". First I zapped some digging to let
the more interesting monsters come closer, then I read a scroll of
taming while confused. The resulting 20 or so pets made it possible
to displace-approach the stairs quite safely. Playing a dance with
my magic missile I easily managed to let my pets block the stairs
as soon as the arch-liches left to try to come close to me. Then I
left that inhospitable place.

The end of that story was unexciting; in the quest (I think) I found
and identified a scroll of genocide, and since I still had no MR I
genocided all L's before I returned to clear the castle.

